  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find $2det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1)=5\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,\u27f9\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+3det(B)=2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0=10.$",
